    <activity>
        <p>
            <term>Work in Groups</term>.
        </p>

        <p>
            Discuss how approximation is used in everyday life such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>measuring length and height,</li>
            <li>money and banking,</li>
            <li>construction work,</li>
            <li>scientific measurements,</li>
            <li>distance and travel.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            Each group should complete the following tasks.
        </p>
        <p>

            <ol marker="(a)">
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Measure the length of a desk, width of a book, or height of a door using a ruler or tape measure.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Record the actual measurement.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Approximate the measurement to:
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <ol marker="(i)">
                            <li>
                                <p>
                                    The nearest whole number.
                                </p>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <p>
                                    <m>1</m> decimal place.
                                </p>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                                <p>
                                    <m>2</m> significant figures.
                                </p>
                            </li>
                        </ol>
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Calculate the absolute error for each approximation.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Identify which approximation gives the smallest error.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Discuss situations where large approximation errors may cause problems.
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </p>

        <p>
            Each group should present:
        </p>
        <p>
            <ol marker="(i)">
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Their measurements?
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Their approximations?
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        The calculated errors?
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Their conclusions on accuracy?
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </p>
    </activity>

